---
import DocsLayout from "../_components/DocsLayout.bangala"
import CodeBlock from "../_components/CodeBlock.bangala"

const page = [
  "---",
  'import Counter from "../components/Counter.bangala"',
  "---",
  "<h1>Dashboard</h1>",
  "<Counter start={10} client:load />",
].join("\n");

const mount = [
  "export async function mount(el, props, ctx) {",
  "  let count = props.start ?? 0;",
  '  const button = el.querySelector("button");',
  "",
  '  button.addEventListener("click", () => {',
  "    count++;",
  "    button.textContent = `count=${count}`;",
  "  });",
  "}",
].join("\n");

const manual = [
  'import { hydrate } from "bangala/client";',
  "",
  "hydrate(document, {",
  "  onError(error) {",
  "    console.error(error.code, error.entry);",
  "  },",
  "});",
].join("\n");

const layout = [
  "components/",
  "  Counter.bangala      # server HTML (the SSR shell)",
  "  Counter.client.ts    # browser code: exports mount()",
  "pages/",
  "  index.bangala        # <Counter start={10} client:load />",
].join("\n");

const headings = [
  { id: "model", label: "Model" },
  { id: "client-module", label: "Client module" },
  { id: "strategies", label: "Strategies" },
  { id: "mount-contract", label: "Mount contract" },
  { id: "errors", label: "Errors" },
  { id: "manual-hydration", label: "Manual hydration" },
];
---
<DocsLayout
  title="Islands Architecture | bangala.js"
  description="Hydratation explicite dans bangala.js avec client:load, client:idle et client:visible."
  path="/docs/islands"
  section="Core Concepts"
  lead="Bangala renders everything to HTML first. Islands are the small pieces you explicitly wake up in the browser."
  headings={headings}
  prev={{ href: "/docs/components", label: "Components" }}
  next={{ href: "/docs/routing", label: "File-based Routing" }}
>
  <h2 id="model">Model</h2>
  <p>A component without a client directive renders to static HTML and ships no client module. Add <code>client:load</code>, <code>client:idle</code>, or <code>client:visible</code> and the compiler emits a <code>&lt;bangala-island&gt;</code> marker with props, entry, and strategy.</p>
  <CodeBlock filename="pages/index.bangala" code={page}/>

  <h2 id="client-module">Client module</h2>
  <p>An island's browser code lives next to its component: <code>Counter.bangala</code> is hydrated by <code>Counter.client.ts</code> (or <code>.tsx</code>, <code>.mts</code>, <code>.js</code>, <code>.jsx</code>, <code>.mjs</code>). The dev server serves it as source, and <code>bangala build</code> bundles only the islands your pages actually use into <code>assets/islands/</code>. Pages without islands ship no JavaScript at all: the runtime is only added where a <code>&lt;bangala-island&gt;</code> appears.</p>
  <CodeBlock filename="project layout" lang="text" code={layout}/>

  <h2 id="strategies">Strategies</h2>
  <table class="docs-table">
    <thead><tr><th>Directive</th><th>Hydrates</th><th>Use for</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>client:load</code></td><td>Immediately.</td><td>Critical above-the-fold controls.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>client:idle</code></td><td>When the browser is idle, with a timeout fallback.</td><td>Secondary widgets.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>client:visible</code></td><td>When the island nears the viewport.</td><td>Below-the-fold charts, comments, embeds.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2 id="mount-contract">Mount contract</h2>
  <p>The browser module exports <code>mount(el, props, ctx)</code>. <code>el</code> is the island marker with the SSR HTML still inside it, <code>props</code> is parsed JSON, and <code>ctx</code> includes <code>strategy</code> and <code>entry</code>.</p>
  <CodeBlock filename="components/Counter.client.js" lang="js" code={mount}/>

  <h2 id="errors">Errors</h2>
  <p>Hydration failures are observable through <code>console.error</code>, <code>data-hydration-error</code>, an optional <code>onError</code> callback, and a bubbling <code>bangala:island-error</code> event.</p>

  <h2 id="manual-hydration">Manual hydration</h2>
  <p>The dev server and the build add <code>bangala/client/auto</code> to pages that contain islands. Custom integrations can call <code>hydrate()</code> directly, and a hand-written <code>&lt;bangala-island data-entry="/islands/x.js"&gt;</code> marker still works for modules served from <code>public/</code>.</p>
  <CodeBlock filename="client.js" lang="js" code={manual}/>
</DocsLayout>
